# RFC-0002: Zenith Interdomain Bus Protocol (ZIB)

**Status:** Draft  
**Version:** 0.3.1  
**Authors:** Surface Zenith Architecture Team  
**Date:** 2026-10-23

---

## Abstract

This RFC defines the Zenith Interdomain Bus (ZIB) — the unified message-passing protocol replacing COM, Binder, Named Pipes, D-Bus, and RPC in the Surface Zenith OS.

## Wire Format

```
Frame {
    magic:       [u8; 4],   // "ZIB\x03"
    version:     u8,        // 1
flags:       u8,        // COMPRESSED | ENCRYPTED | FRAGMENTED | LAST_FRAG
    payload_len: u32,       // big-endian
    checksum:    u32,       // CRC32-like
    sequence:    u64,       // per-session sequence number
    reserved:    [u8; 4],
    payload:     [u8],      // bincode-encoded ZMessage
}
```

## Topic Contract

All topics are strongly typed (no raw strings). Each topic has:
- A defined payload schema
- A default TTL
- A QoS policy (AtMostOnce / AtLeastOnce / ExactlyOnce)
- A priority weight

## QoS Policies

| Policy       | Delivery       | Ordering    | TTL      | Retries |
|--------------|----------------|-------------|----------|---------|
| BestEffort   | AtMostOnce     | Unordered   | 5s       | 0       |
| Reliable     | AtLeastOnce    | PerSource   | 30s      | 3       |
| ExactlyOnce  | ExactlyOnce    | GlobalOrder | ∞        | 10      |
| RealTime     | AtMostOnce     | PerSource   | 100ms    | 0       |
| Security     | ExactlyOnce    | GlobalOrder | ∞        | 5       |

## Security

Publishing to capability-required topics requires a valid CapabilityToken in the message header. The ZIB validates tokens before delivery.

## Syscall Interface

```
zib_publish(session_id, topic_id, source_domain, payload, payload_len, ttl_ms) → i64
zib_subscribe(topic_id, domain_id, out_sub_id) → i64
zib_recv(sub_id, buf, buf_len, out_msg_len) → i64
zib_send_directed(session_id, topic_id, source, target, payload, len) → i64
```
